        "reason": "The analogy accurately maps electron transfer to a game of catch where one party throws (loses) and the other catches (gains) the ball (electron).",
        "errors": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "u3",
      "kind": "STUDY_SUPPORT",
      "label": "OIL RIG mnemonic for oxidation and reduction",
      "excerpts": [
        {
          "text": "In high school chemistry, the easiest way to remember what is happening to the electrons is a simple phrase:\n\n> **OIL RIG**\n> *   **O**xidation **I**s **L**oss (of electrons)\n> *   **R**eduction **I**s **G**ain (of electrons)",
          "occurrence": 0
        }
      ],
      "attributes": {
        "subtype": "mnemonic"
      },
      "contextualization": {
        "value": "none",
        "evidence": []
      },
      "accuracy": {
        "verdict": "accurate",
